AX6 LED schedule
================

LuCI:
  System -> LED 定时开关

UCI:
  uci set ax6_led.schedule.enabled=1
  uci set ax6_led.schedule.on_time=07:00
  uci set ax6_led.schedule.off_time=23:00
  uci set ax6_led.schedule.days='1 2 3 4 5 6 7'
  uci set ax6_led.schedule.leds='blue:system blue:network yellow:system yellow:network'
  uci commit ax6_led
  /etc/init.d/ax6-led-schedule restart

Semantics:
  ON  window: all configured LEDs are forced ON (default-on, max brightness)
  OFF window: all configured LEDs are forced OFF (trigger none, brightness 0)
  Enabled=0: restore the normal LED state captured before scheduling / normal LED service

Manual:
  ax6-led-schedule status
  ax6-led-schedule off
  ax6-led-schedule on
  ax6-led-schedule restore
  ax6-led-schedule run

When on_time > off_time the ON window crosses midnight.
Days use 1=Monday ... 7=Sunday; empty means every day.
